# cross-lib-activity-collision — Lib A (the referring policy library).
library "Root".

// Root's decision recommends BOTH sibling libraries' `Deny` activities. Since
// `recommendationIdForLib(metadata, "Deny")` is scoped to the POLICY id (not the
// library), SharedA."Deny" and SharedB."Deny" both emit an ActivityDefinition and
// Recommendation PlanDefinition at the SAME canonical URL / id. Whole-closure
// activity-name uniqueness is therefore REQUIRED; the duplicate must trip a
// closure collision invariant (Inv 0 closure-resource-url-collision / Inv 1
// closure-resource-collision) and sink success — never silently pick a winner.

concept "Condition A":
- type is Condition.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `condition-a`.

concept "Condition B":
- type is Condition.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `condition-b`.

decision "Triage":
- when "Condition A" then recommend activity "SharedA"."Deny".
- when "Condition B" then recommend activity "SharedB"."Deny".
